  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342117",
      "title": "Type Inference & Type Casting",
      "lectureOrder": 498,
      "videoOrder": 440,
      "sourceHash": "b056d0420df32b4a3d0327af4ed26f16025d841d4a61ff9e28f2fbf16f24e00a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 4.27,
          "en": "Okay let's now wire up our function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.27,
          "end": 6.02,
          "en": "to our formula.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.02,
          "end": 8.81,
          "en": "For that, I'll add IDs to those inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.81,
          "end": 9.963,
          "en": "num1 and num2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.64,
          "end": 14.3,
          "en": "so that in our app.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.3,
          "end": 16.811,
          "en": "we can get access to those elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.811,
          "end": 19.31,
          "en": "Num1Element is for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.31,
          "end": 22.011,
          "en": "accessed with document getElementById, num1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.011,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "That's some default JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 26.69,
          "en": "which we can run in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.69,
          "end": 29.29,
          "en": "And that's the next important takeaway.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.29,
          "end": 31.73,
          "en": "TypeScript builds up on JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.73,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "This means that any JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 36.29,
          "en": "works in TypeScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.29,
          "end": 38.92,
          "en": "You can learn TypeScript by simply sticking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.92,
          "end": 42.94,
          "en": "to what you know and then you add types step by step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.94,
          "end": 45.06,
          "en": "maybe you find some place where you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 47.59,
          "en": "some advanced TypeScript feature you heard about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.59,
          "end": 48.46,
          "en": "But in a nutshell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 48.46,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "you can always just write JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 55.47,
          "en": "and it will work because TypeScript builds upon JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.47,
          "end": 58.663,
          "en": "All JavaScript code is supported in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.43,
          "end": 63.92,
          "en": "Therefore, we can use this regular JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.92,
          "end": 66.25,
          "en": "for selecting the num1Element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.25,
          "end": 70.37,
          "en": "We can duplicate this to get access to the num2Element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.37,
          "end": 72.92,
          "en": "We can get access to our button element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.92,
          "end": 76.11,
          "en": "by reaching out to the button with document querySelector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.11,
          "end": 78.40299999999999,
          "en": "and selecting the first button which we find.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 82.7,
          "en": "And then we can add a listener, an eventListener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.901,
          "end": 87.11,
          "en": "to button element by calling addEventListener on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.11,
          "end": 88.803,
          "en": "Add a click event listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.28999999999999,
          "end": 93.5,
          "en": "And to find a function that should execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.5,
          "end": 95.53,
          "en": "when the button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.53,
          "end": 97.58,
          "en": "Now something interesting you see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.58,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "is that my ID knows that I can call addEventListener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 103.92,
          "en": "on the button element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.92,
          "end": 105.55,
          "en": "To ask this might be clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.55,
          "end": 107.5,
          "en": "we know that we select a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.5,
          "end": 109.46000000000001,
          "en": "and we know that the button DOM element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.46000000000001,
          "end": 111.69,
          "en": "has the AddEventListener method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.69,
          "end": 116.69,
          "en": "But why does my ID notice in the end because of TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.02000000000001,
          "end": 119.87,
          "en": "because it knows that when we select a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.87,
          "end": 121.55,
          "en": "with querySelector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.55,
          "end": 124.083,
          "en": "what we'll get back is an HTMLButtonElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.33,
          "end": 128.34,
          "en": "If I hover over a button element you see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.34,
          "end": 132.13,
          "en": "that's something which is called the inferred type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.13,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "We didn't define this type explicitly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 138.94,
          "en": "I didn't add colon HTMLButtonElement here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.94,
          "end": 140.35,
          "en": "though I could.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.35,
          "end": 142.18,
          "en": "But we don't need to do this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.18,
          "end": 145.55,
          "en": "because TypeScript is able to infer types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.55,
          "end": 147.79,
          "en": "And it's really smart regarding that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.79,
          "end": 150.47,
          "en": "it's able to find out which type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.47,
          "end": 153.16,
          "en": "will eventually be stored in this constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.16,
          "end": 155.51,
          "en": "because of this code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.51,
          "end": 157.223,
          "en": "And that's pretty nice of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.15,
          "end": 161.15,
          "en": "So it knows will eventually have a button in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.15,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "and that's why it knows that we can call addEventListener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.296,
          "end": 168.187,
          "en": "Now here inside the event listener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.187,
          "end": 169.51,
          "en": "I now want to extract the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 169.51,
          "end": 172.1,
          "en": "from num1 and num2 element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.1,
          "end": 176.713,
          "en": "So here I got my num1 are reaching out to num1Element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.09,
          "end": 182.753,
          "en": "And then there I want to access the value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.13,
          "end": 186.573,
          "en": "Now my ID does not like this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 191.21,
          "en": "The reason for that is, that not every HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.21,
          "end": 193.28,
          "en": "has a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.28,
          "end": 195.97,
          "en": "Input elements have value properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.97,
          "end": 198.51,
          "en": "paragraphs for example, don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 201.13,
          "en": "So we need to convince TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.13,
          "end": 204.95,
          "en": "that what we get access to here will be an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.95,
          "end": 206.84,
          "en": "For the button, it knew that it's a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.84,
          "end": 209.4,
          "en": "because we query select by the button tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.4,
          "end": 211.13,
          "en": "Here, we select by ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 211.13,
          "end": 213.57999999999998,
          "en": "so TypeScript has no chance of knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.57999999999998,
          "end": 216.53,
          "en": "which kind of element it will have those IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 216.53,
          "end": 218.84,
          "en": "But we can do something else related to types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 218.84,
          "end": 221.28,
          "en": "which is called type costing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "If we as a developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 228.02,
          "en": "know with certainty that something is of a certain type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.17000000000002,
          "end": 230.36,
          "en": "we can use the special ask keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.36,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "which is added by TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 234.82,
          "en": "to tell TypeScript that what we select here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 234.82,
          "end": 236.6,
          "en": "will be off that type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 236.6,
          "end": 240.79,
          "en": "And here it will be off the HTMLInputElement type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 240.79,
          "end": 243.54,
          "en": "We can do this on both these elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 243.54,
          "end": 245.823,
          "en": "Now these types here, HTMLInputElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 247.025,
          "end": 248.42,
          "en": "HTMLButtonElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 248.42,
          "end": 250.62,
          "en": "These are general types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 250.62,
          "end": 252.89,
          "en": "which are built into TypeScript so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 252.89,
          "end": 254.22,
          "en": "You can always use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 256.07,
          "en": "just like you can use number ends on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.07,
          "end": 258.07,
          "en": "These are some general DOM types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 258.07,
          "end": 260.97,
          "en": "which are available in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 260.97,
          "end": 264.02,
          "en": "And with that now, we can access value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 264.02,
          "end": 265.88,
          "en": "because now we know that there will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.88,
          "end": 269.45,
          "en": "a value property on this DOM object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 269.45,
          "end": 272.963,
          "en": "We also get num2 with num2Element.value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 273.87,
          "end": 275.95,
          "en": "And now we can call add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 275.95,
          "end": 277.67,
          "en": "or we can get our result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 277.67,
          "end": 281.04,
          "en": "by calling add and passing in num1 and num2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 281.04,
          "end": 284.21,
          "en": "And now again, TypeScript saves our --.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 284.21,
          "end": 286.31,
          "en": "This is the bug I mentioned earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 286.31,
          "end": 288.29,
          "en": "which would be easy to introduce.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 288.29,
          "end": 290.7,
          "en": "You get the value entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 290.7,
          "end": 292.63,
          "en": "And since user enters numbers here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 292.63,
          "end": 295.38,
          "en": "you expect that you get numbers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 295.38,
          "end": 300.38,
          "en": "But value actually always returns a string here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 300.45,
          "end": 302.76,
          "en": "That's the return type of this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 302.76,
          "end": 305.2,
          "en": "It's the type of value stored in this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 305.2,
          "end": 310.173,
          "en": "And this is always under all circumstances, a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 311.09,
          "end": 313.44,
          "en": "Now here we need numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 313.44,
          "end": 316.71,
          "en": "So here, the fix is easy, we converted this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 316.71,
          "end": 319.83,
          "en": "But now we are forced to make that conversion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 319.83,
          "end": 323.572,
          "en": "and we can't forget or overlook it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 323.572,
          "end": 325.36,
          "en": "And that's all TypeScript is about in a nutshell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 325.36,
          "end": 327.803,
          "en": "We are forced to write cleaner code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 328.72,
          "end": 332.4,
          "en": "Well, and then I can console log the result here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 337.4,
          "en": "With all of that, let's again run TSC app.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 337.81,
          "end": 339.76,
          "en": "this compiles to code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 339.76,
          "end": 341.39,
          "en": "If we have a brief look at the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 341.39,
          "end": 343.65,
          "en": "you'll see the -- operators gone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 343.65,
          "end": 345.17,
          "en": "all the types are gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 345.17,
          "end": 346.53,
          "en": "So does this JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 346.53,
          "end": 348.18,
          "en": "we could have written on our own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 348.18,
          "end": 351.7,
          "en": "but this is no code which was checked in advanced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 351.7,
          "end": 355.23,
          "en": "during development here in our TypeScript version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 355.23,
          "end": 358.22,
          "en": "And now if I reload here, and I enter five and 11,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 358.22,
          "end": 362.937,
          "en": "we get 16 and not unintended 115 or 511,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 364.14,
          "end": 368.033,
          "en": "because now we were forced to add this type conversion here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
